Docker Engine and container tools

Install:
  Install missing Docker packages and NVIDIA container support when an NVIDIA GPU is present.
  On a new engine installation, enable and restart Docker and configure user access.

Upgrade:
  Update installed Docker and NVIDIA container packages, retaining service and proxy settings.

Status:
  Read installed package versions, service state and proxy configuration.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a running systemd instance; root or sudo.

Configuration:
  Proxy: optional HTTP proxy at 127.0.0.1, configured during a new engine installation.
  Existing proxy settings are retained. Leave the port empty to skip; --yes does not answer this prompt.
  NO_PROXY defaults include localhost, Docker host, and private networks.
  Existing daemon.json is retained. Apply new GPU runtime settings by restarting Docker.
  Docker group membership grants root-equivalent access; log in again to apply it.
